# Apical hook opening, biologically parameterised
# Walia A., Carter R., Wightman R., Meyerowitz E.M., Jonsson H., Jones A.M.
# (2024) Dev Cell 59:3245-3258
#
# The epidermis is a closed, turgid, centre-triangulated TRBS shell. Growth is
# Lockhart wall yielding, gated by the TWO chemical signals the paper measures
# and finds are "depleted upon illumination": auxin (represses extension) and
# wall alkalinity (acidification permits it). Neither gate sets the
# inner/outer differential - acidification happens on both flanks, and the
# inner flank carries MORE auxin yet grows more. The differential instead
# comes from each cell's remaining elongation capacity: all hook epidermal
# cells mature to the same length, and outer-flank cells are born near it.
#
# Wall material is dynamically anisotropic (Eq. 3): the fibre stiffness
# redistributes onto the maximal principal stress direction, which is the
# model's prediction of CMT orientation.
#
# units: um, hours.  Cell vars: 0-2 stress dir, 3 anisotropy, 4 sigma1,
#                               5 auxin, 6 acid, 7 type, 8 theta
11 0 0

CenterTriangulation::Initiate 0 1 1
9       # CT data appended after the 9 cell variables

VertexFromTRBScenterTriangulation 3 3 1 1 1
20000.0 # Y_mod: isotropic matrix modulus (pectin/hemicellulose).
        #   Y, Y_fiber and P are scaled together so the elastic
        #   strains are unchanged but mechanical relaxation is fast
        #   compared with growth (overdamped vertex drag otherwise
        #   lets the walls grow without the organ unrolling).
0.3     # P_ratio
0.02    # stress-state refresh interval (h)
0       # wall length index
9       # CT start index
0       # store stress state at 0 -> dir on VTK cell-vector, aniso on its length

WallMechanics::FiberSpring 3 2 1 1
1350.0  # Y_fiber: CMT-guided cellulose, redistributed by Eq. 3
0.7     # K_hill (paper: k = 0.7)
1.2     # n_hill (paper: n = 1.2)
0       # wall length index
0       # cell stress-state start index

Pressure3D::CenterTriangulation 1 1 1
17.5    # P_force (turgor per unit shell area)
9       # CT start index

WallGrowth::AcidGrowth 6 5 1 1 1 1 1
9.0    # @GROWTH k_growth (per unit strain per h)
0.005   # strain_threshold (Lockhart yield strain)
0.55    # K_auxin: auxin level at half-repression
6       # n_auxin
0.45    # K_acid: acidification at half-activation
3       # n_acid
0       # wall length index
5       # cell auxin index
6       # cell acid index
1       # wall growFlag (axial walls only)
3       # wall Lmax index (mature cell length)

CenterTriangulation::WallGrowth::StrainSaturationHill 6 2 1 1
9.0    # @GROWTH_CT k_growth: internal edges follow the surface
0.005   # strain_threshold
30.0    # L_max for internal edges
0.55    # K_Hill (auxin)
4       # n_Hill
0       # hill_flag: repressing
9       # CT start index
5       # cell auxin index

Degradation::One 1 1 1
0.5     # @AUXIN_DECAY k_d: light-triggered auxin depletion (t=0 = light);
        #   tau = 2 h, so the gates release over the first ~2 h and the
        #   hook barely moves before then, as measured
5       # cell auxin index

Creation::Zero 1 1 1
2.0     # @ACID_DRIVE acidification; with the relaxation below gives
        #   acid = 1 (measured: both flanks acidify within 30 min of light)
6       # cell acid index

Degradation::One 1 1 1
2.0     # @ACID_RELAX relaxation rate (sets tau with the drive above)
6       # cell acid index

VertexNoUpdateFromIndex 0 1 16
# Clamp the apical end-cap ring (ring 32, cotyledon end): the hook unrolls
# about the apex and the basal shank swings out into the straight axis.
512 513 514 515 516 517 518 519 520 521 522 523 524 525 526 527
InnerTissue::GrowingCore 2 1 1
0.025   # @CORE sub-epidermal core elongation rate (per h); the paper's
        #   subepidermal longitudinal force sL. Raising it accelerates both
        #   hook opening and the anisotropy switch (their Fig 4F).
1e4     # penalty stiffness: the core resists compression, cannot pull
1       # wall variable flagging the axial walls the core bears against
